ies)","status":"pending","priority":"high"},{"content":"Implement server.py (MCP server with tools)","status":"pending","priority":"high"},{"content":"Write BDD GWT PyTest tests","status":"pending","priority":"high"},{"content":"Run tests and verify build","status":"pending","priority":"high"}],"truncated":false},"title":"6 todos","time":{"start":1782088841632,"end":1782088841633}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"The guide is the same as TASK.md. Let me plan the implementation.\n\nI'll build:\n1. `pyproject.toml` / setup\n2. `src/brazilian_soccer_mcp/` package with:\n   - `data_loader.py` - load CSVs, normalize team names, dates\n   - `queries.py` - query functions for matches, teams, players, competitions, stats\n   - `server.py` - MCP server exposing tools\n3. `tests/` - BDD GWT PyTest tests\n\nLet me keep it simple but complete. I'll use fastmcp since it's available.\n\nLet me design the modules.\n\nData loader:\n- Normalize team names: strip state suffix \"-SP\", lowercase compare, handle accents (keep but compare normalized)\n- Parse dates: ISO and DD/MM/YYYY\n\nLet me write the code.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_eecc5b99c0012TLU4hSI5xGjvt","sessionID":"ses_1133b0fc9ffeCrHgypJPQ5E9ps","messageID":"msg_eecc587770015q989oUTGXgRC1"}}
