{"type":"text","timestamp":1782089306821,"sessionID":"ses_1133b0fc9ffeCrHgypJPQ5E9ps","part":{"id":"prt_eecccc6e7001FzfIWjiBbAWyZg","messageID":"msg_eecccb9d2001dRAyDyFEL4zTqw","sessionID":"ses_1133b0fc9ffeCrHgypJPQ5E9ps","type":"text","text":"Done. Implemented the Brazilian Soccer MCP server per `TASK.md`.\n\n**Structure**\n- `pyproject.toml` — package config, deps (pandas, mcp, fastmcp), console script `brazilian-soccer-mcp`.\n- `src/brazilian_soccer_mcp/data_loader.py` — loads all 6 CSVs, normalizes team names (strips `-UF` suffixes, parentheticals, accents), parses multiple date formats, produces a unified matches DataFrame + FIFA players DataFrame.\n- `src/brazilian_soccer_mcp/queries.py` — query functions covering all 5 required categories: matches, teams, players, competitions, statistics.\n- `src/brazilian_soccer_mcp/server.py` — FastMCP server exposing 13 tools.\n- `tests/` — BDD GWT (Given/When/Then) tests with pytest-bdd, one feature file per category.\n\n**Results**\n- Package installs cleanly (`pip install -e .`).\n- All 19 BDD tests pass.\n- All 13 MCP tools verified callable (`list_competitions`, `last_match_between`, etc.).\n- 23,954 matches and 18,207 players load successfully across all datasets.\n\nRun the server with `brazilian-soccer-mcp` or `python -m brazilian_soccer_mcp.server`.","time":{"start":1782089303783,"end":1782089306820}}}
